{
  "reportDate": "2026-11-13",
  "scope": "Complete validation reuse after synchronized apply and scoped full-read decoding allocations",
  "methodology": [
    "Release arm64 synthetic tests in a signed private native host. No real clicks, installed application/data access or real account/endpoint participates.",
    "The first engine experiment alternates three fresh-process old/new runs on byte-identical 20k SQLite copies. Before packages are archived from 2f5fc372; after packages match the final package source manifest. Engine initialization and UI preparation are outside that timer.",
    "The native inventory uses the unchanged generated fixture workload at 10k/20k with three trials per operation: fourteen windows, 84 unique samples. Cold means empty application/archive/engine caches; the OS disk cache is not purged.",
    "Native seed creation, repository/index setup, assertions and frame painting are outside timers. Store time includes result admission and scheduling browse invalidation, not later page painting.",
    "The new post-apply seed uses a real verified empty/uninitialized remote window followed by normal apply prepare/commit. It preserves local corpus counts, semantic nodes and history. The fixture removes derived certificate metadata immediately before this completely checked writer, which must issue the replacement.",
    "After closing that engine, both control cases copy the same committed database. One retains its certificate; the other deletes only that derived row before the timer. Both time the same capture into fresh archives and check saved state/history. This is a current-binary controlled comparison, not a timing of the old binary after sync.",
    "All sync preparation/validation and copy/control setup occur outside the post-apply favorite timers. These measure avoiding a repeated preparation after work has already been checked; they do not make initial sync validation free.",
    "The common twelve native windows are compared with the preceding independently generated workload. The extra two setup/windows change process/cache history before full-store readiness; use the byte-identical engine experiment to attribute the decoder improvement.",
    "Medians/minima/maxima describe three observations, not percentiles. Engine and native store milestones are different and their absolute timings should not be added or substituted.",
    "The full 43-operation inventory was not rerun. Image-heavy/dense-alias workloads retain focused correctness coverage rather than large-library timings."
  ],
